a young girl who disappeared more than  two years ago in central new york has  been found alive police found paisley  schultes in this secret compartment  under the stairs in a home that they had  searched before officials say the little  girl was abducted by her biological  parents after they lost custody of her  our national correspondent rica duncan  shows us now how one detective paying  very close attention made the startling  discovery  after two years of searching detectives  finally found paisley schultes and this  home in saugertis new york huddled in a  small wet space beneath a staircase one  of my detectives was walked up and down  the steps a number of times during the  course of the search and he said it was  just something about the steps that was  off he used a flashlight and where two  of the step boards came together he  looked through the crack and he saw what  he believed was a blanket eventually  they saw a pair of little feet and when  they got more boards off they found the  little girl paisley  the girl now six years old was  discovered with her mother kimberly  cooper police believe cooper and the  girl's father kirk schultz jr kidnapped  paisley after losing custody of her in  2019  investigators had been to the home  before it belonged to the girl's  paternal grandfather but investigators  say a fresh tip led them to believe the  child was being hidden inside the  residence on monday officers arrived  with a search warrant they were adamant  with our officers that the child was not  there which led me to believe after the  fact that they had done this so many  times and gotten away with it both  biological parents along with paisley's  grandfather were arrested and are now  facing several charges including  endangering the welfare of a child  paisley is in good health and was  reunited with her older sister and legal  guardian for cbs mornings jerica duncan  new york  it's a very ugly story uh the police  also said that the little girl had not  been taught to read or write she's now  six and if you've ever had a  six-year-old you know it's not easy to  get them to do anything let alone get  under a stare and then be hammered in  quiet and then stay quiet that's that's  not a pretty picture i'm curious to know  why they lost stories of missing kids  usually don't end with them being found  she is safe and alive we're happy about  that as awesome
 

